# Supabase Setup Guide

Follow these steps to connect your app to Supabase:

## 1. Create Supabase Project
- Go to https://supabase.com and sign up/log in
- Click "New Project"
- Enter a project name (e.g., "money-management")
- Choose a region close to you
- Set a strong database password
- Wait 2-3 minutes for project to initialize

## 2. Run Database Migration
- In Supabase dashboard, go to **SQL Editor**
- Click **New Query**
- Copy the contents of `supabase/migrations/001_init.sql` from this repo
- Paste into the editor and click **Run**
- Wait for success message

## 3. Get Your Credentials
- Go to **Project Settings** → **API**
- Copy **Project URL** (looks like `https://xxxxx.supabase.co`)
- Copy **anon public** key (under "Project API keys")

## 4. Create `.env.local` File
In the root of this project, create a file named `.env.local` and add:

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://idjqepckscqspoegkzaw.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImlkanFlcGNrc2Nxc3BvZWdremF3Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODE3NDEwMjIsImV4cCI6MjA5NzMxNzAyMn0.ZkTnKyb7w2bXvGYO0U30B3YhbA4PoWLR5tutCUYbuUA

# AI features (Financial Assistant + receipt scanning).
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com → API Keys.
# Receipt scanning ALWAYS uses Claude (it needs vision), so this key is
# required for that feature regardless of the chat provider below.
# Without it, the AI features return a friendly "not configured" message;
# the rest of the app works normally.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Which model powers the chat assistant: "claude" (default) or "deepseek".
# DeepSeek runs the CHAT ONLY — it has no vision, so receipt scanning stays on
# Claude either way.
ASSISTANT_PROVIDER=claude

# Required only when ASSISTANT_PROVIDER=deepseek. Get a key at
# https://platform.deepseek.com. Optionally override the model
# (defaults to deepseek-v4-flash; deepseek-v4-pro is the higher-quality tier).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# Bank-statement import parses a multi-page PDF on a stronger Claude model
# (uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Override the model here if needed.
STATEMENT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
```

Replace the values with your actual credentials from step 3.

## 5. Install Supabase Client
```bash
pnpm install @supabase/supabase-js
```

## 6. Restart Dev Server
```bash
pnpm dev
```

## 7. Test
- Navigate to http://localhost:3000
- Click "Add Transaction" on the dashboard
- Fill in the form and submit
- Your transaction should appear in the list

## Troubleshooting

**"Error: Missing Supabase credentials"**
- Make sure `.env.local` file exists in the project root
- Restart dev server after creating `.env.local`

**"Error: Cannot find module '@supabase/supabase-js'"**
- Run `pnpm install @supabase/supabase-js`

**"Error: RLS policy violation"**
- Make sure the SQL migration ran successfully (check Supabase SQL Editor for any errors)

## Notes

- The mock user ID is hardcoded as `'user-1'` for now (no authentication required)
- You can upgrade to real user auth later by replacing the hardcoded user_id
- All data is scoped to the mock user_id, so test data won't conflict with real users
